PTY FIXTURE ISOLATION

The combined targeted run passed 9 library and 15 MCP tests, but exposed
existing 2-second PTY shutdown guards while all eight seat scenarios ran
together. First the unavailable-socket cleanup failed; after explicit cooked
EOF, the hangup cleanup failed. Both real failures remain in
targeted-initial-failure.log and targeted-second-failure.log.
The hangup test passed alone and the original three PTY cases passed together;
their logs are pty-isolated.log and pty-group.log.
No functional deadline was relaxed. The unavailable-socket test now sends
explicit EOF, and scripts/test.py runs the five launcher scenarios in a
separate invocation from the PTY lifecycle cases. Every case still executes;
there is no global test lock or change to product scheduling. The full
canonical gate verifies both invocations.

